
# Home Lab Hardware Inventory

## 1. Purpose

This document records the physical hardware used or planned for this home lab.

It provides a central reference for:

- Identifying installed hardware.
- Recording hardware specifications.
- Tracking purchased and planned equipment.
- Checking component compatibility.
- Documenting firmware and BIOS/UEFI settings.
- Recording hardware health and test results.
- Planning upgrades.
- Tracking maintenance and warranties.

This inventory should describe the actual equipment in the lab. Do not enter assumed specifications. If a value is unknown, use `To be verified`.

---

## 2. Inventory Status Definitions

Use these statuses consistently throughout this document.

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Planned | Equipment is being considered but has not been purchased. |
| Ordered | Equipment has been purchased but has not arrived. |
| Acquired | Equipment has arrived but has not been installed. |
| Installed | Equipment has been physically installed. |
| Verified | Equipment has been installed and its operation has been tested. |
| Retired | Equipment is no longer in active use. |

