### CPU Verification Checklist

- [ ] Identify the exact CPU model.
- [ ] Confirm the number of physical cores.
- [ ] Confirm the number of threads.
- [ ] Check virtualization support.
- [ ] Check IOMMU support if required for device passthrough.
- [ ] Confirm motherboard socket compatibility.
- [ ] Confirm BIOS/UEFI compatibility.
- [ ] Check cooling requirements.
- [ ] Record the manufacturer's specifications.

### Why Virtualization Support Matters

Virtualization allows one physical server to run multiple virtual machines.

Examples of possible lab workloads include:

- Linux server virtual machines.
- Windows test environments.
- Network simulation systems.
- Application development environments.
- Database servers.
- Infrastructure services.

CPU virtualization support is important when using platforms such as KVM, Proxmox VE or other hypervisors.

