| Cooling | Temperature monitoring under load | Not tested | — | Pending |
| UPS | Controlled backup-power test | Not tested | — | Pending |
| Overall system | Sustained stability test | Not tested | — | Pending |

### Testing Principles

- Use reliable diagnostic tools.
- Record the test conditions.
- Record errors rather than hiding them.
- Do not run destructive storage tests on drives containing important data.
- Back up important information before testing.
- Monitor temperatures during stress testing.
- Stop testing if temperatures, noise or system behaviour indicate a potential hardware problem.

