## 15. Power Consumption and Operating Cost

A home lab can run for many hours each day. Power consumption should be measured rather than guessed.

| Measurement | Value |
|---|---|
| Idle power draw | Not measured |
| Typical operating power | Not measured |
| Peak power draw | Not measured |
| Measurement device | To be recorded |
| Measurement date | Not measured |
| Average operating hours per day | To be recorded |
| Electricity tariff | To be verified |
| Estimated monthly energy consumption | Not calculated |
| Estimated monthly electricity cost | Not calculated |

### Basic Energy Calculation

Energy consumption:

`Energy (kWh) = Power (kW) × Operating hours`

For example, a server drawing an average of 100 watts for 24 hours:

`0.1 kW × 24 hours = 2.4 kWh per day`

Estimated monthly consumption over 30 days:

`2.4 kWh × 30 = 72 kWh per month`

Estimated monthly electricity cost:

`Monthly energy consumption (kWh) × applicable electricity tariff`

Use your actual measured power draw and applicable tariff. The example is illustrative, not a prediction of your server's consumption.

